    "description": {
      "value": "<p>An unsealed letter, its wax seal already broken, taken from one of the dead travellers. It is addressed in a careful hand to someone in <strong>Daggerford</strong> — the paper gone soft from folding and unfolding on the road, the ink smudged at one corner. The few lines inside are an ordinary letter home: that the roads had been kind, that the writer hoped to be back before the first frost, and that there was nothing to worry about.</p>",
